{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you","id":1465158,"title":"[Union games] How dark to make the Technocracy around you?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-24T10:29:01-07:00","id":1465158,"title":"[Union games] How dark to make the Technocracy around you?","content":"I should note I'm primarily a Technocrat player. When I share this online, I tend to get a bit of disbeief because I often am the first in line to talk about Union abuses and making them a dangerous Orwellian organization. A lot of gamers assume that I want to make the Union one-dimensional or that I am a fan of 1st Edition Technocrats. Quite the contrary. The Guide to the Technocracy is my all time favorite supplement.<br /> <br /> However, it comes with the caveat that my games would be RUINED if the Technocracy's <i>leadership</i> wasn't evil. I am a huge fan of <i>La Femme Nikita</i>, <i>Nowhere Man</i> (The Bruce Greenwood series), <i>The X-Files</i>, and <i>Day of the Condor</i>. Which is to say that I am very fond of the idea the player characters are good guys trapped in a situation where they are working for the bad guys but there's no good alternative.<br /> <br /> Usually, when introducing the concept, I explain like such:<br /> <br /> 1. You can be effective.<br /> 2. You can be moral.<br /> 3. You can be rich.<br /> <br /> Pick two.<br /> <br /> <b>CT Phipps' Technocracy</b> is the single most effective organization in the World of Darkness for holding back the night. Even more than werewolves, it is there to deal with incursions of ghosts, zombies, demons, Nephandi, Maruaders, and baby-snatching Lost Ones that don't care the Middle Ages are over. It is also guilty of state-sponsored terrorism, murder, brainwashing, torture, kidnapping, and genocide. The latter including plans to exterminate all supernaturals, their Kinfolk, Kinian, and followers. If you read the Technocracy's history, they're always one step behind virtually every Western colonialist power and believing it's all justified in enlightening the world. They're not like that anymore (albeit some still hold those views because your boss' boss is a former Dutch East India company executive) but that's because people PUSHED BACK.<br /> <br /> <b>Can it be saved?</b><br /> <br /> <b>Is it better than the alternative?</b><br /> <br /> <b>Is it the only game in town?</b><br /> <br /> Part of what I enjoy about Technocrat games is that they're very useful for a lot of moral questions. One adventure may be to get take down a pedophile murderer Ronin Garou (The Nappy Napper from Project: Twilight) and the next to be to forcibly recruit a 12 year old Dreamspeaker that has been kidnapped from his family. The morality of the latter one is the <i>point</i> and seeing how players react to being told he's going through Room 101. Do they let him go? Do they erase his memory of his past lives? Do they willingly betray their fellow agent who wants to kill the &quot;thing&quot; in a body of a child?<br /> <br /> Like <i>La Femme Nikita</i> the series, the player characters are as much working against their superiors as they are the Traditions. You need to play the game, assassinate, gather blackmail information, accumulate power, and increase your magical power to eventually become head of the Union yourself because that's the only way anything is going to change. In WW2, the Union was supporting fascism until half of them revolted and destroyed the other half.<br /> <br /> Surely it's not going to take THAT to save it again, right?<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> So how dark should the Union be if you're a Technocrat? We've got a lot of different versions of it with the horrible Null-B to the Guide to the Technocracy to Iteration X's apologia for the Technocracy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T10:50:52-07:00","id":1465166,"title":"","content":"This, of course, depends on the kind of story you're trying to tell. One reason why I prefer the less unified Union that premiered in Mage revised is because it makes it easier to ignore the corrupt elements in the Union if they'd get in the way of the story you're trying to tell. That said, I'm more willing to willing to go with CTPhipp's Technocracy if it's not the only game in town for Enlightened Scientists. See my various rants in the past about Navalon; and I'd also point you to the <a href=\"https://mobunited.livejournal.com/48488.html\" target=\"_blank\">Transhuman Adepts</a> from Malcolm Sheppard's <a href=\"https://mobunited.livejournal.com/58878.html\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: the Sterile Version</a> \u2014 which, incidentally, has a lot of insights on how to play and run the Technocracy, albeit from back in the days when they were still assumed to be antagonists by default. In particular, it delves into just what failing Malcolm sees the Technocracy featuring, as well as his assessment as to why there's so much interest in trading the Technocracy as good guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T11:18:48-07:00","id":1465170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1465166#post1465166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This, of course, depends on the kind of story you're trying to tell. One reason why I prefer the less unified Union that premiered in Mage revised is because it makes it easier to ignore the corrupt elements in the Union if they'd get in the way of the story you're trying to tell. That said, I'm more willing to willing to go with CTPhipp's Technocracy if it's not the only game in town for Enlightened Scientists. See my various rants in the past about Navalon; and I'd also point you to the <a href=\"https://mobunited.livejournal.com/48488.html\" target=\"_blank\">Transhuman Adepts</a> from Malcolm Sheppard's <a href=\"https://mobunited.livejournal.com/58878.html\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: the Sterile Version</a> \u2014 which, incidentally, has a lot of insights on how to play and run the Technocracy, albeit from back in the days when they were still assumed to be antagonists by default. In particular, it delves into just what failing Malcolm sees the Technocracy featuring, as well as his assessment as to why there's so much interest in trading the Technocracy as good guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, I always felt like part of the problem was treating the Sons of Ether as jokes with no actual scientists among them. I feel like that was a missed opportunity.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T12:07:02-07:00","id":1465172,"title":"","content":"My personal problem is with the idea of a monolithic Technocracy. Simply put, I can't buy it. I know how big organizations work. I've studied them for decades and I've been working at one for 6 years while observing its inner workings.<br /> <br /> So, for me, beneath the surface few things actually apply to the whole Union. There are amalgams empowered to employ a small army of state-of-the-art HIT Marks at any problem and receiving frequent, detailed missions. And there are amalgams with an old carcass of a Mark V and a can of spray paint that they can make work sometimes if they try hard, and the only communication they get from higher ups is their salaries and semestral reviews limited to checking if any problem went to the local newspaper. If not, every one gets a free pen.<br /> <br /> Two key concepts to understand large organizations are Middle Management and Resource Allocation. Middle Management means that between the highest higher ups and the factory floor there are many cogs, and those cogs<b><u> aren't</u></b> just for show. Upper Management can't actually manage most aspects of the organization, otherwise this micromanaging overwhelms them easily. So most decisions that affect your life are actually taken by Middle Management and there is where the organization &quot;happens&quot;. The most well-meaning Upper Management is frequently powerless in face of the very structure that allows bad Middle Management to happen.<br /> <br /> Resource Allocation means that enough resources isn't a thing for an organization, ever. It doesn't matter how much you have, your global work by definition uses up everything and some. You have to start new projects, you have to deal with logistics, you have to pay for your entire existence. And you have to send this money and other resources to every cranny and nook. All the while accounting for losses of all kinds, and counting, again, on a lot of Middle Management.<br /> <br /> Large organizations are fragmented and self diverse. Both their best and their worse are depending on where you look. They are also conflicted, but in a very complex way, not simply as &quot;your boss is evil&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T13:10:28-07:00","id":1465176,"title":"","content":"I suppose that there could be some Primal Utility Adjustments that could allow a massive organization to operate more efficiently; but the ones that could really make a difference are probably Vulgar, Coincidental but subject to the Domino Effect, or some sort of Wonder with all the difficulties of creation and maintenance that that implies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T13:44:01-07:00","id":1465178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1465176#post1465176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose that there could be some Primal Utility Adjustments that could allow a massive organization to operate more efficiently; but the ones that could really make a difference are probably Vulgar, Coincidental but subject to the Domino Effect, or some sort of Wonder with all the difficulties of creation and maintenance that that implies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, I just assumed that during the Cold War that half of the NWO was working against the other half.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T14:55:49-07:00","id":1465182,"title":"","content":"My Technocracy is still recovering from the disaster of the avatar storm. The Union Directorate (situated on earth, they are the &quot;temporal&quot; leaders of the union, an emergency committee formed by representatives of the most influential symposia, at least till contact with the Masters is reestablished) has its hands full with the recovery efforts, which leaves them with little time and resources to spare, something that they try desperately to hide. The illusion of Control must be maintained, or the whole Union falls into chaos.<br /> <br /> The darkness comes from the fact that many amalgams are not sure whose timetable they're following. The chaos of the avatar storm has been used by some technocrats (nephandi, greedy assholes, and other malcontents) to turn their symposiums into their personal kingdoms. The Directorate can do little about it since purging a symposium would lower moral, expose a weakness to their enemies and leave the Union without much-needed resources. This is something that the rogue technocrats know and exploit, leaving the Directorate no choice but to reach a usually unfavorable agreement with them.<br /> <br /> Constant paranoia is a must in a technocray game, but here is ramped up by the fact that, more than ever before, you receive contradictory orders from many sources and all claim to be the ultimate authority of the Union. It's hard enough to do your job without having to second guess every order that you receive because you could be harming the Union without knowing it. But even if you find out your boss is a traitor, what can you do? Hell, should you do something? It's your ass on the line... Then again, nobody said being an agent of a global conspiracy would be easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 10-28-2021, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T15:52:49-07:00","id":1465200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1465176#post1465176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose that there could be some Primal Utility Adjustments that could allow a massive organization to operate more efficiently; but the ones that could really make a difference are probably Vulgar, Coincidental but subject to the Domino Effect, or some sort of Wonder with all the difficulties of creation and maintenance that that implies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought about it and I assume it is done. But at the same time the Union is exponentially more complex with all the hyperbolic conspiracy, Umbra Constructs and Enlightened Science. Add to it rival managers using the same effects, and although it does work it isn't a big change in the larger scale.<br /> <br /> You could say that the very fact that this organization still stands is a miracle at this point.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T21:49:26-07:00","id":1465241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you#post1465158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how dark should the Union be if you're a Technocrat? We've got a lot of different versions of it with the horrible Null-B to the Guide to the Technocracy to Iteration X's apologia for the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were storytelling a Technocratic Union campaign, I would use some of the same Technomancer NPC motivations and plots as I do for my ongoing Traditions Chronicle. There's a group of them who want to totally extract the Appalachia Mountain Range and build huge Arcologies with the resources taken. In advance of gentrifying a city, they targeted youth likely to be affected - and thus in the way - and got them all hooked on steroids and amphetamines. They are attempting to involve a Tradition Mage in building a total-surveillance drug rehab facility so they can move the unwanted population out of the way of affluent tech workers (effectively human trafficking). A Progenitor Mage tricked a kid into drowning so she could resuscitate him by injecting a foreign organism into his lungs. She later apologized to one of the PCs, saying she was only following orders.<br /> <br /> I make antagonists rationally self-interested, afflicted by Quite (usually Clarity), ideological in the mundane sense and, as a last resort, evil (nature: sadist). On the other hand, many Union NPCs are pursuing genuinely positive goals and some are actually powerful. In a Technocracy Chronicle, I would prefer the players looking up at the top of the hierarch and wondering which bosses are evil rather than being able to simply conclude that the whole leadership is evil. The solution to pure corruption at the top is Revolution.<br /> <br /> It might be interesting to put the worst Technocrats all in one Amalgam in a city close the Construct from which the players are operating. They know the whole group is bad, but they bring in revenues, have a high standing in the Union and firmly control their territory.<br /> <br /> Syndicate - Financier: Runs a payday loan company that charges 800% interest. <br /> NWO - Watcher: Runs a revenge-porn website. <br /> Iteration X - TMM: Runs a prison labor contracting company. <br /> Progenitor - Genegineer: Sells anti-aging gene therapy to the city oligarchs.<br /> Void Engineer - R&amp;E: Defense contractor building orbital weapons platforms and killer satellites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T11:11:32-07:00","id":1465674,"title":"","content":"I don't need the leadership of the Technocracy to be evil, per se, I need them to be detached. I don't need the Technocracy to be evil, per se, I need them to be corrupt in specific ways. <br /> <br /> Plenty of forms of corruption plague the Technocracy, but I think there are three specific ones that define its dark side for me: Noble cause corruption (the pursuit of ideals to such a degree that you sacrifice ideals), institutional corruption (the temptation for the organization to protect itself at the expense of its purpose), and systemic corruption (flaws in the structure that encourage personal corruption).<br /> <br /> Between those three you have the push for individual amalgams to do monstrous things in the pursuit of technocracy goals, the inescapable reality of favor trading and graft, a leadership willing to ignore or even endorse both, and a resulting culture of silence. That's everything I need to explain most of the states the Technocracy can be in.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T15:18:28-07:00","id":1465839,"title":"","content":"The social interaction that happens between Technomancers in a hierarchy usually happens in a specific context, that of being in a Construct, be it Deep Umbral or Earthly. I did a Google Search of the forum to see if there were any posts about how different storytellers map out Constructs. Couldn't find any (they could be hiding from my novice Google-Fu). I started a \u200b<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465563-technocracy-construct-design-for-raids-or-as-player-home-base\">Post</a> about Constructs. I didn't post any of my ideas as I wanted to leave it somewhat open ended. The <i>Place</i> where Technocrats spend downtime is important to how characters internalize faction-culture and conform to the agendas of powerful antagonists. If you want to sneak into the lab of a demented Bio-Mechanic, it helps if the storyteller has a map.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T14:24:07-07:00","id":1465942,"title":"","content":"I have been wondering about the Technocracy and Jhor. Killing large numbers of sleepers with Magick is something the Technocracy does when it suits an important goal. One of the more advanced symptoms of this form of Quite is an obsession with wanting to bring down the Shroud, a nice plot device for introducing Wraith NPCs into your setting. It's hard to imagine a Technomancer doing this, but it is easy to imagine that quite a few would be sufficiently afflicted to want to do it. I suppose they would have to pass themselves off as normal long enough to convince a Void Engineer to teach them Dimensional Science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T15:47:18-07:00","id":1465944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1465942#post1465942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been wondering about the Technocracy and Jhor. Killing large numbers of sleepers with Magick is something the Technocracy does when it suits an important goal. One of the more advanced symptoms of this form of Quite is an obsession with wanting to bring down the Shroud, a nice plot device for introducing Wraith NPCs into your setting. It's hard to imagine a Technomancer doing this, but it is easy to imagine that quite a few would be sufficiently afflicted to want to do it. I suppose they would have to pass themselves off as normal long enough to convince a Void Engineer to teach them Dimensional Science.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since I assume union agents go through regular psychological and physical exams (and even more after dangerous missions), and since the union has been doing it for several decades now, I'm pretty sure that the screening process would pick almost every agent afflicted by Jhor. The few that manage to escape don't tend to stay hidden for long, since their obsession eventually leads them to commit a mistake. The problem is how much damage they inflict before they are discovered, and a cunning mage can cause a lot of damage. One could have the crazy idea of going to the labyrinth in the underworld and detonate a spirit nuke, but that would never happen...right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T17:07:43-07:00","id":1465948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1465944#post1465944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since I assume union agents go through regular psychological and physical exams (and even more after dangerous missions), and since the union has been doing it for several decades now, I'm pretty sure that the screening process would pick almost every agent afflicted by Jhor. The few that manage to escape don't tend to stay hidden for long, since their obsession eventually leads them to commit a mistake. The problem is how much damage they inflict before they are discovered, and a cunning mage can cause a lot of damage. One could have the crazy idea of going to the labyrinth in the underworld and detonate a spirit nuke, but that would never happen...right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the Nephandi are extremely good at infiltrating and the Technocracy has a hole section of their people who don't BELIEVE in the Spirit/Dimensional Science Sphere. Mind you, a big question is how much you want to portray 1st Edition Union corruption as still accurate (or an exaggeration) because 1st Edition Union had the Special Projects Division, Iteration X corrupted by the Machine God, and other incredible screw ups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T17:23:36-07:00","id":1465951,"title":"","content":"Point of clarification: only in Mage Revised is Jhor a form of Quiet. Before and after, Jhor is a kind of Resonance. This was, in fact, one of the motivations behind renaming the three quiets in M20, where Clarity became Denial and Jhor became Morbidity. Jhor <i>could</i> cause a Morbid Quiet, or not; the coupling between Resonance and Quiet is fairly lax. So even if Morbidity causes the mage to want to tear down the Shroud, that still doesn't mean that using Magick to kill means that you'll go Morbid.<br /> <br /> Edit: I would also suggest that the Technocracy's tendency to rely on Devices means that agents are less likely to develop Resonance of <i>any</i> sort: an agent shooting you with a BFG-2000 isn't performing a Procedure or an Adjustment, and so technically isn't \u201cusing <s>Magick</s>Science to kill you\u201d. The BFG-2000 itself, OTOH, is a different story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-30-2021, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T17:42:50-07:00","id":1465956,"title":"","content":"Even without 1st edition screw ups, the screening process isn't necessarily all that effective. Psychological screenings aren't an easy thing, and Mage vs Mage pretty much means that for every tool at the Union's disposal to pick up problems, there's something else to scramble it.<br /> <br /> The first big challenge on a screening is separating what is just your usual human weirdness. Normal, healthy people are already a strange bunch up close, and psychologists know this. Then the second challenge is defining what exactly you picked up, because similar symptoms can signal vastly different problems, with just as different prognostics and treatment.<br /> <br /> So between a problem starting and it being properly identified and isolated a lot of time can pass and since Enlightened Agents aren't a dime a dozen simpler risk assessments are more likely to determine one of them staying on duty than an adequate diagnosis.<br /> <br /> After all, think about it, despite all the effort they make to appear bland and uniform to the Traditions the fact is that they stay Mages, and Mages aren't a wholesome bunch. Between researchers going to work dressed like Kirk and Field Agents that swear an adaptation of the Oath of the Templars, the Union's psychologist knows that you can't normalize those weirdos without killing their precious Genius, so you have to live with it.<br /> <br /> I'd say a smart agent with Jhor can go a long way if they're just good enough at concealment. It wouldn't be necessarily easy, certainly harder than in the Traditions, just because of internal structure, but definitely it is doable to stay on the top of your game while hiding your unhealthy death obsession from the Union.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T17:44:48-07:00","id":1465958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1465951#post1465951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point of clarification: only in Mage Revised is Jhor a form of Quiet. Before and after, Jhor is a kind of Resonance. This was, in fact, one of the motivations behind renaming the three quiets in M20, where Clarity became Denial and Jhor became Morbidity. Jhor <i>could</i> cause a Morbid Quiet, or not; the coupling between Resonance and Quiet is fairly lax. So even if Morbidity causes the mage to want to tear down the Shroud, that still doesn't mean that using Magick to kill means that you'll go Morbid.<br /> <br /> Edit: I would also suggest that the Technocracy's tendency to rely on Devices means that agents are less likely to develop Resonance of <i>any</i> sort: an agent shooting you with a BFG-2000 isn't performing a Procedure or an Adjustment, and so technically isn't \u201cusing <s>Magick</s>Science to kill you\u201d. The BFG-2000 itself, OTOH, is a different story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did have it questioned just how many Technocrats actually existed once because it was impossible to tell the difference between their Hedge Mages, regular scientists, and Enlightened personnel to outsiders.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T18:03:45-07:00","id":1465960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1465951#post1465951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: I would also suggest that the Technocracy's tendency to rely on Devices means that agents are less likely to develop Resonance of <i>any</i> sort: an agent shooting you with a BFG-2000 isn't performing a Procedure or an Adjustment, and so technically isn't \u201cusing <s>Magick</s>Science to kill you\u201d. The BFG-2000 itself, OTOH, is a different story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if their actual Enlightened personnel are as reliant on Devices as it seems. Any &quot;prototype&quot; of a new model or whole new Device is enough to have it as Instrument instead of an actual Device, and there are many Procedures that rely on more-or-less standardized Instruments that, for an external observer, can't be distinguished from a Device.<br /> <br /> As much as they are, indeed, more common in the Union, I'd say they are not actually the standard fare for true Mages that can McGuiver their way through improvised tools or have their own prototypes for personal use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T10:09:41-07:00","id":1466669,"title":"","content":"My opinion is that while there are some good crats (the Void Engineers are mostly ok in my book), there's an awful lot of them, especially in the Syndicate and NWO, who are in dire need of the Good Death.<br /> I was always a bit icked out by later editions whitewashing the crats. It's like removing the skull symbols from a Waffen-SS uniform and replacing them with Hello Kitty buttons. The cute exterior doesn't change the fact that it's an abomination that needs to burn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1631-karthak","name":"Karthak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1631_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T10:22:15-07:00","id":1466671,"title":"","content":"The M20 position on that appears to be more along the lines of \u201cclean up your own mess first\u201d. The Traditions aren't exactly pillars of virtues, either; and it's the height of hubris for them to go crusading against the Union when they've got their own issues to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T10:54:28-07:00","id":1466679,"title":"","content":"That's usually an argument for when Side A has the same flaws as Side B. That's not really the case here. The typical Tradition flaws are that they are too reactive, they are behind the times, they are too fractious, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T11:11:50-07:00","id":1466684,"title":"","content":"Actually, that's the Disparate Alliance. The Traditions flaws are more along the lines of only being interested in Sleepers in the context of Awakening them, and otherwise showing a callous disregard for them. Other than that, their main interest is in personal Ascension at all costs. That, and perhaps they're a little <i>too</i> inclusive, to the point of being reticent to criticize each other, even when it may be warranted, because \u201cthat's just the way he does things, and I'd be a hypocrite to presume that my way is better\u201d. <br /> <br /> And that's exactly as fair a characterization of the Traditions as \u201cthe Technocracy is an abomination that needs to burn.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-04-2021, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T11:44:26-07:00","id":1466689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466684#post1466684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, that's the Disparate Alliance. The Traditions flaws are more along the lines of only being interested in Sleepers in the context of Awakening them, and otherwise showing a callous disregard for them. Other than that, their main interest is in personal Ascension at all costs.<br /> <br /> And that's exactly as fair a characterization of the Traditions as \u201cthe Technocracy is an abomination that needs to burn.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Disparate Alliance is more reactionary than reactive. The Traditions have a vision for the future that they are working towards and it isn't like the past and in that sense they are quite radical. What I meant was that while individual Traditionalists are quite active in advancing that goal, I find the organization itself to be quite passive. As a group they react to new developments rather than drive them. Some of that is my own impression I am sure, though I find it a natural outgrowth of the setting as we know it. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T15:31:40-07:00","id":1466708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karthak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466669#post1466669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My opinion is that while there are some good crats (the Void Engineers are mostly ok in my book), there's an awful lot of them, especially in the Syndicate and NWO, who are in dire need of the Good Death.<br /> I was always a bit icked out by later editions whitewashing the crats. It's like removing the skull symbols from a Waffen-SS uniform and replacing them with Hello Kitty buttons. The cute exterior doesn't change the fact that it's an abomination that needs to burn.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, I'm not sure this is what <i>whitewashing</i> means. I may be wrong.<br /> <br /> Second, the Traditions:<br /> <br /> 1- accept a bunch of assholes that think that <u><b>judging and killing</b></u> others out of how they live their lives is fine, not only their right but divine mandate;<br /> <br /> 2- want a world where being druid-like is grounds to justify <b><u>human sacrifices</u></b>;<br /> <br /> 3- have several members that at one point or another engaged in religious persecution and genocide;<br /> <br /> 4- protect ludite reactionaries that want to bring down all technology and the safety and health of common people be damned;<br /> <br /> 5- think that your right at doing your thing far outweighs any concern at seeing if your individual Ascension is harming innocents. It is against the law, but who's going to watch?<br /> <br /> So, who are the right people in the game?<br /> <br /> The answer exists and is <i>individuals</i>. Mage is a game about individual will and power, where every character have the power to do good or evil as they define it.<br /> <br /> None of the organizations is beyond accepting problematic shit in their midst for their greater cause, and none is devoid of good members that can take on their hands to correct what's wrong without and within.<br /> <br /> And yes, <b>1st Edition</b>went the route of making one of them outright good and the other outright evil. If you want to follow that path, you're welcome. But there's a reason <i>many players don't think it fair to equate the only of the two trying to make modern medicine reliable to Nazis</i>.<br /> <br /> It is a game with many themes and many interpretations on them, your view isn't the only possible take from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T15:41:51-07:00","id":1466709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466708#post1466708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, I'm not sure this is what <i>whitewashing</i> means. I may be wrong.<br /> <br /> Second, the Traditions:<br /> <br /> 1- accept a bunch of assholes that think that <u><b>judging and killing</b></u> others out of how they live their lives is fine, not only their right but divine mandate;<br /> <br /> 2- want a world where being druid-like is grounds to justify <b><u>human sacrifices</u></b>;<br /> <br /> 3- have several members that at one point or another engaged in religious persecution and genocide;<br /> <br /> 4- protect ludite reactionaries that want to bring down all technology and the safety and health of common people be damned;<br /> <br /> 5- think that your right at doing your thing far outweighs any concern at seeing if your individual Ascension is harming innocents. It is against the law, but who's going to watch?<br /> <br /> So, who are the right people in the game?<br /> <br /> The answer exists and is <i>individuals</i>. Mage is a game about individual will and power, where every character have the power to do good or evil as they define it.<br /> <br /> None of the organizations is beyond accepting problematic shit in their midst for their greater cause, and none is devoid of good members that can take on their hands to correct what's wrong without and within.<br /> <br /> And yes, <b>1st Edition</b>went the route of making one of them outright good and the other outright evil. If you want to follow that path, you're welcome. But there's a reason <i>many players don't think it fair to equate the only of the two trying to make modern medicine reliable to Nazis</i>.<br /> <br /> It is a game with many themes and many interpretations on them, your view isn't the only possible take from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very Technocratic point of view.<br /> <br /> Effectively, you have adopted the stance that the Traditions are people who are still trying to bring back the Mythic Age and revert humanity to the moral systems of the heyday of the cultures that the Traditions are from. Which I think is something the Technocracy argues the Traditions are trying to do but is absolutely something that they made up with rare exceptions. The Traditions are people that are possessed of moral compasses informed by both the Modern world and their own syncretic progressiveness that generally moves past the culture of Sleepers around them.<br /> <br /> 1st Edition Mage portrays them as the good guys because, well, they are. They aren't against science, they have their own police force to fight evil, and they are people that are trying to show the poor and impoverished masses that the drug companies are suppressing the CURE FOR CANCER because it turns out that you actually can cure it with a magic potion brewed for six days in the woods.<br /> <br /> 3# is also particularly weird because the Technocracy is the one who was behind, in-universe, the genocide of native peoples across the globe and had to have a revolt by its own members because they decided to side with the Axis. The Allied Technocrats won but they were a revolution against what was depicted as an inherently pro-fascist culture. A lot of people felt that was offensive but the original inspiration for the Order of Reason's heyday was the BRITISH EMPIRE and Queen Victoria as the founder of the Union. Their associations with colonialism are baked into their DNA.<br /> <br /> I know plenty of people who want to make the Celestial Choir into a bunch of knight templar fanatics but they literally have the religion of, &quot;There are many roads to God and none of them are wrong.&quot; Which is pretty much the antithesis of fundamentalism as we know it.<br /> <br /> The Union makes a lot of propaganda about the Traditions being a bunch of anti-vaxxer religious fanatics and nuts but that's never been anything but propaganda because THOSE PEOPLE DON'T AWAKEN.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T16:11:24-07:00","id":1466717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466708#post1466708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, I'm not sure this is what <i>whitewashing</i> means. I may be wrong.<br /> <br /> Second, the Traditions:<br /> <br /> 1- accept a bunch of assholes that think that <u><b>judging and killing</b></u> others out of how they live their lives is fine, not only their right but divine mandate;<br /> <br /> 2- want a world where being druid-like is grounds to justify <b><u>human sacrifices</u></b>;<br /> <br /> 3- have several members that at one point or another engaged in religious persecution and genocide;<br /> <br /> 4- protect ludite reactionaries that want to bring down all technology and the safety and health of common people be damned;<br /> <br /> 5- think that your right at doing your thing far outweighs any concern at seeing if your individual Ascension is harming innocents. It is against the law, but who's going to watch?<br /> <br /> So, who are the right people in the game?<br /> <br /> The answer exists and is <i>individuals</i>. Mage is a game about individual will and power, where every character have the power to do good or evil as they define it.<br /> <br /> None of the organizations is beyond accepting problematic shit in their midst for their greater cause, and none is devoid of good members that can take on their hands to correct what's wrong without and within.<br /> <br /> And yes, <b>1st Edition</b>went the route of making one of them outright good and the other outright evil. If you want to follow that path, you're welcome. But there's a reason <i>many players don't think it fair to equate the only of the two trying to make modern medicine reliable to Nazis</i>.<br /> <br /> It is a game with many themes and many interpretations on them, your view isn't the only possible take from it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This a hundred times.<br /> <br /> That's why I always emphasize to my players that ethics and morality are, despite the influence of the group they belong to, ultimately a personal matter for each mage. You want to play as the good guys? Then stop looking at the groups because they sure as hell aren't innocent, and they're never going to be perfect. Instead, look at yourself in the mirror, you're the one who has to decide to be, and act, like a good person. The mage is the one who has to change reality and make a difference, that's why they're a frigging mage in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T16:11:52-07:00","id":1466718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Union makes a lot of propaganda about the Traditions being a bunch of anti-vaxxer religious fanatics and nuts but that's never been anything but propaganda because THOSE PEOPLE DON'T AWAKEN. </div> </div> </div>Sure they do! There's nothing that says that your Focus needs to be a healthy one in order to Awaken; and some absolute loons have Awakened in the past. Why should that change just because there's no real-world basis for anti-vaxxing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T16:13:07-07:00","id":1466719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466718#post1466718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure they do! There's nothing that says that your Focus needs to be a healthy one in order to Awaken; and some absolute loons have Awakened in the past. Why should that change just because there's no real-world basis for anti-vaxxing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it depends on how open-minded and enlightened you have to be to Awaken in the view of the ST. I figure that fanatics, fundamentalists, and the incredibly close-minded would be the least likely to awaken.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T16:26:08-07:00","id":1466722,"title":"","content":"Awakening doesn't require being open-minded or enlightened; all that's required is a strong will, a Paradigm, a Practice, and Instruments. Oh, and the involvement of an Avatar; that's the mystery ingredient that's the lynchpin to the whole process. Let me remind you that some Etherite theories make anti-vaxxing seem tame. And given that business about will, fanaticism strikes me as something that's likely to <i>increase</i> your chances of Awakening.<br /> <br /> One might say that that's the core of the horror in Mage: the Phenomenal Cosmic Power that they're granted doesn't discriminate in who gets the power; and the people you detest the most are just as likely to Awaken as the people you revere the most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-04-2021, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T17:55:40-07:00","id":1466729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466709#post1466709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a very Technocratic point of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course it is. The point isn't to say that the Traditions are wrong and the Union are right, but to say that both can be framed as such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466709#post1466709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Effectively, you have adopted the stance</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong. I didn't said any of this as being the whole of the Traditions, but as being something in them.<br /> <br /> The Euthanatoi are a sore point, though, because they are, by all means, criminal extremists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466709#post1466709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which I think is something the Technocracy argues the Traditions are trying to do but is absolutely something that they made up with rare exceptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>So criticism on the Traditions is made-up bullshit and criticism on the Union isn't?<br /> <br /> The point with the change in the Union outlook in the books is to retcon them into their past display being as much Tradition propaganda as the things I pointed are Technocratic propaganda.<br /> <br /> Yes, this is a retcon, the whole point is that 2nd edition retconed the Union because a lot of players thought their original concept is stupid. It isn't a matter of enlightened understanding of their original purpose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466709#post1466709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Traditions are people that are possessed of moral compasses informed by both the Modern world and their own syncretic progressiveness that generally moves past the culture of Sleepers around them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not by a large margin, but changing <b>slowly</b> to become like you say.<br /> <br /> The original Traditions are <b><u>extreme</u></b> Ludites. Modernists among them were few and politically weak. No write-up of them before Revised ever shown technologically inclined members as more than a weak minority outside the Technomancer Traditions.<br /> <br /> First edition Trads are proud Ludites with very few modernists as weird outliers. Second edition are grumbling Ludites with vocal modernist minorities. Revised is where modernists <i><b>start </b></i>to become common, but the leadership is still very Ludite (as Revised liked to throw insider fight between young and old in every line). Only M20 opens up the possibility of making Ludite members into a hyper-conservative minority.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466709#post1466709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1st Edition Mage portrays them as the good guys because, well, they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course they are, this isn't real life, the authors can make anyone objectively good or evil.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466709#post1466709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They aren't against science,</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1st ed the <b><u>Players</u></b> aren't expected to be against science if they don't want to. The bulk of the Traditions pretty much are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466709#post1466709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> they have their own police force to fight evil</div> </div> </div> </div>So does the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466709#post1466709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the drug companies are suppressing the CURE FOR CANCER</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, in the 1st ed setting they are and this is due to Technocracy shenanigans.<br /> <br /> This isn't necessarily true in late 2nd and Revised, and I'm aware this is a retcon. There is the possibility that the Union simply isn't achieving to make a cure for Cancer because they're as limited by the Consensus as everyone else. So they have cures, <i><b>but not reliable, safe ones</b></i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466709#post1466709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> because it turns out that you actually can cure it with a magic potion brewed for six days in the woods.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you can't. Here's the catch.<br /> <br /> With their focus on personal Ascension, the Traditions' many paradigms focus on personal knowledge and craft.<br /> <br /> It pretty much means that A) the potion can't be brewed by everyone, only by a properly trained individual and B) it can't be mass produced. So while it is a thing, this cure simply isn't easily available.<br /> <br /> Of course, modernists (those people that aren't standard before M20) do accept also scientific development that can solve this, and <i>some</i> even encourage and include it in their Paradigms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466709#post1466709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3# is also particularly weird because the Technocracy is the one who was behind, in-universe, the genocide of native peoples across the globe</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as the Celestial Chorus have a core belief of &quot;all faiths are good&quot;, in practice many of them had a hand in the Inquisition and on many other religious persecutions through history.<br /> <br /> Many of the Trads have a history of conflict among themselves or even among their inner factions, out of religious persecution. Bloody conflicts.<br /> <br /> Either the Traditions are genocidal assholes or the Union may learn from past mistakes. You can't hold past mistakes against one and just pardon the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466709#post1466709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their associations with colonialism are baked into their DNA.</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as the Choir association with witch-hunts, the Verbena association with human sacrifices, the Hermetic association with demonology, and so on.<br /> <br /> They can all outgrow it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466709#post1466709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know plenty of people who want to make the Celestial Choir into a bunch of knight templar fanatics</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is wrong, but that doesn't change that they existed (and still do in very small numbers), and the Choir had a number of serious schisms and factional wars because of theological differences through their history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466709#post1466709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Union makes a lot of propaganda about the Traditions</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course they do. And it is reciprocated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466709#post1466709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THOSE PEOPLE DON'T AWAKEN.</div> </div> </div> </div>From where did you even got this bullshit conclusion!?<br /> <br /> It is a big point in the game that all sorts of people Awaken and that despite great efforts from all sides to find the truth of the matter, no one ever fund any reliable correlation between cause and effect for Awakenings.<br /> <br /> This is, unfortunately, pretty much not true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466719#post1466719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose it depends on how open-minded and enlightened you have to be to Awaken in the view of the ST. I figure that fanatics, fundamentalists, and the incredibly close-minded would be the least likely to awaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, have you considered that this runs contrary to your own view on the Technocracy?<br /> <br /> The game never made any assertion in this regard and have plenty of NPCs that pretty much are fanatics, fundamentalist and incredibly close-minded, all over the place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T18:05:17-07:00","id":1466731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466729#post1466729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First of all, have you considered that this runs contrary to your own view on the Technocracy?<br /> <br /> The game never made any assertion in this regard and have plenty of NPCs that pretty much are fanatics, fundamentalist and incredibly close-minded, all over the place.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy will never be remotely like real fascists or dictatorships. Because the Technocracy, unlike RL monsters, actually want to do what they do because they believe it is for the betterment of society.<br /> <br /> All mages, even Nephandi, are fundamentally selfless.<br /> <br /> The Nephandi just believe the experiment in existence needs to end.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T05:42:15-07:00","id":1466763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466731#post1466731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Technocracy will never be remotely like real fascists or dictatorships. Because the Technocracy, unlike RL monsters, actually want to do what they do because they believe it is for the betterment of society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that there was a time where fascism was heralded in American periodicals for the good it could do for society. I think it was even in Time magazine, oddly enough.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, real life monsters often do things in the name of the betterment of society. Lobotomies, eugenics, ethnic cleansing, human sacrifice, forced sterilization, the reign of terror... And to bring this back around to the current discussion, many of those things were also supported by significant chunks of the Technocracy. I don't think they are representative of the Technocracy per se, but it is important to point out that the desire for a better society is not a protection against going off the rails.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T06:22:52-07:00","id":1466764,"title":"","content":"And that's setting aside the fact that mages are every bit as likely to be self-centered as anyone else. The Awakened are not more ethical than Sleepers. They are not more sane than Sleepers. They are not smarter than Sleepers. They are not wiser than Sleepers. They are not more altruistic than Sleepers. And despite the name of the Technocratic power stat, they are not more enlightened than Sleepers \u2014 not in the sense that most people use the term, anyway. The only sense in which they are more enlightened is that they know how to bend the world to their will. <br /> <br /> By any yardstick other than sheer power and drive, mages are no better than Sleepers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-05-2021, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T06:48:46-07:00","id":1466767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466764#post1466764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's setting aside the fact that mages are every bit as likely to be self-centered as anyone else. The Awakened are not more ethical than Sleepers. They are not more sane than Sleepers. They are not smarter than Sleepers. They are not wiser than Sleepers. They are not more altruistic than Sleepers. And despite the name of the Technocratic power stat, they are not more enlightened than Sleepers \u2014 not in the sense that most people use the term, anyway. The only sense in which they are more enlightened is that they know how to bend the world to their will.<br /> <br /> By any yardstick other than sheer power and drive, mages are no better than Sleepers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly disagree. The Traditions and Technocracy are absolutely not like any RL organization that wields its kind of power. They are about many things but never enforcing a rigid caste for power. They are both fundamentally selfless organizations.<br /> <br /> Which is rarer than roc's teeth.<br /> <br /> But hey, that's just my take.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T10:07:07-07:00","id":1466783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466729#post1466729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as the Celestial Chorus have a core belief of &quot;all faiths are good&quot;, in practice many of them had a hand in the Inquisition and on many other religious persecutions through history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of. Once you get to the 800's most of the persecution seems largely driven by the Cabal of Pure Thought. While I'm sure the Chorus did use its influence to drive out certain religions and philosophies, they would be clear targets of the Inquisition.<br /> Honestly the history of the Chorus doesn't work for me. I think the abrahamic/monotheistic Tradition should have the kind of history you indicate. I just think the Chorus isn't the right philosophy for that, nor does it work as a driving force behind the spread of Christianity or Islam. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466767#post1466767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I strongly disagree. The Traditions and Technocracy are absolutely not like any RL organization that wields its kind of power. They are about many things but never enforcing a rigid caste for power. They are both fundamentally selfless organizations.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I associate the three forms of corruption I did with the Technocracy. They don't need to desire power to become a force that enforces it and a system that demands it. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T10:34:59-07:00","id":1466786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466783#post1466783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sort of. Once you get to the 800's most of the persecution seems largely driven by the Cabal of Pure Thought. While I'm sure the Chorus did use its influence to drive out certain religions and philosophies, they would be clear targets of the Inquisition.<br /> Honestly the history of the Chorus doesn't work for me. I think the abrahamic/monotheistic Tradition should have the kind of history you indicate. I just think the Chorus isn't the right philosophy for that, nor does it work as a driving force behind the spread of Christianity or Islam.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Malcolm Sheppard (MRev), the celestial chorus never was the driving force between Christianity or Islam. It was always a heresy. Likewise, according to Malcolm, with every Tradition. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466783#post1466783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why I associate the three forms of corruption I did with the Technocracy. They don't need to desire power to become a force that enforces it and a system that demands it. </div> </div> </div> </div>True; and I will grant that the Technocracy is founded on some very noble ideals \u2014 just like many real-world organizations. But it's also populated by regular human beings, and is liable to do some very immoral things in the pursuit of those ideals \u2014 just like many real-world organizations. Heck, Technocrats are also prone to pay lip service to the Technocracy's higher ideals while pursuing their own selfish interests \u2014 just like many real-world organizations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T10:39:08-07:00","id":1466787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466767#post1466767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I strongly disagree. The Traditions and Technocracy are absolutely not like any RL organization that wields its kind of power. They are about many things but never enforcing a rigid caste for power. They are both fundamentally selfless organizations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most organizations that we see as monstrous are fundamentally selfless. They got as far as they did precisely because they felt morally justified. All we can achieve by refusing to see this is to open the path for the next monstrous organization to do it all again because they're not like their predecessors, &quot;they have a selfless cause&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T10:49:20-07:00","id":1466790,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Of all tyrannies, a tyranny sincerely exercised for the good of its victims may be the most oppressive. It would be better to live under robber barons than under omnipotent moral busybodies. The robber baron's cruelty may sometimes sleep, his cupidity may at some point be satiated; but those who torment us for our own good will torment us without end for they do so with the approval of their own conscience.<br /> <br /> C.S. Lewis</div>That's the Technocracy at its best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T11:11:28-07:00","id":1466794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466790#post1466790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Of all tyrannies, a tyranny sincerely exercised for the good of its victims may be the most oppressive. It would be better to live under robber barons than under omnipotent moral busybodies. The robber baron's cruelty may sometimes sleep, his cupidity may at some point be satiated; but those who torment us for our own good will torment us without end for they do so with the approval of their own conscience.<br /> <br /> C.S. Lewis</div>That's the Technocracy at its best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun fact: CS Lewis described an organization very much like the Technocracy in one of his non-Narnia books. They existed to suppress the supernatural, magic, and control human society by carefully dolling out technology while suppressing most discoveries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-05-2021, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T12:23:50-07:00","id":1466804,"title":"","content":"I don't think it was in The Chronicles of Narnia. But I do recall the NICE from That Hideous Strength, the conclusion of his Ransom trilogy, that was very much like that. The closest you get to that in Narnia was the school that Eustace and Jill attended.<br /> <br /> It's worth mentioning also that technocracy is not a word that Mage invented. \u201cRule by the technical elite\u201d is a very real thing. And my own opinion is that treating Mage's Technocracy as much like its real-world namesake as possible is the way to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T12:48:42-07:00","id":1466807,"title":"","content":"Sorry, it was meant to be non-Narnia. Typo. My bad. I need to stop listening to the Primogen podcasts while I write.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T12:34:19-07:00","id":1466972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466786#post1466786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to Malcolm Sheppard (MRev), the celestial chorus never was the driving force between Christianity or Islam. It was always a heresy. Likewise, according to Malcolm, with every Tradition.<br /> <br /> <br /> True; and I will grant that the Technocracy is founded on some very noble ideals \u2014 just like many real-world organizations. But it's also populated by regular human beings, and is liable to do some very immoral things in the pursuit of those ideals \u2014 just like many real-world organizations. Heck, Technocrats are also prone to pay lip service to the Technocracy's higher ideals while pursuing their own selfish interests \u2014 just like many real-world organizations.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy's ideals also include mass murder. The fifth Precept of Damian is a call to genocide, as is the Declaration of the White Tower, the founding document of the Order of Reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1631-karthak","name":"Karthak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1631_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T13:19:34-07:00","id":1466980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karthak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466972#post1466972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocracy's ideals also include mass murder. The fifth Precept of Damian is a call to genocide, as is the Declaration of the White Tower, the founding document of the Order of Reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes with a caveat and a lot of context.<br /> <br /> The caveat being that most of the terms used on both the Declaration and the Precept are open to interpretation. It doesn't means they didn't meant it when they were first defined, but it does mean that individual members and groups in the Union may have less murderous interpretations and even the Union as a whole may change its instance on them, so they may not have such a strict interpretation today unless the ST wants to.<br /> <br /> After the first batch of Convention books, material on the Technocracy have a tendency to hint that such genocidal readings aren't universal and may not even be standard anymore.<br /> <br /> Context being that the Union know of supernatural beings from their own perspective, and due to everyone's tendency to hold to their secrets, they have no reason to change such perspectives. They are hardly the only group, even if you count on Traditionalists, that see no reason to accept the continued existence of shapeshifting monstrosities that come out of nowhere and murder humans indiscriminately and without reason, for example.<br /> <br /> Many Traditions and Crafts gave them no more reason <i>as a group</i> to think otherwise. What is your proposal on how to deal with a Taftani that fully knows the risks of Paradox to the people around them and yet don't give a shit? Again, just an example. Mage's history is full of moments when those supernatural willworkers were locked on wars of all kinds and just threw their magics around with apparently little regard for others' safety. And that was precisely the kind of conflicts they were in when those rules got made.<br /> <br /> Does any of that means the Union is just right? Of course not. It does mean, though, that the situation is too nuanced to be fair to just say they're monsters, either, and ignore all the other things happening and the other ways they may behave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T21:36:07-07:00","id":1467014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you#post1465158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how dark should the Union be if you're a Technocrat?</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire Union is a ceaseless nightmare of flaming putrescence vomited up by the blackest pits of hell, which still has better HR standards than the Union<br /> <br /> (cough)<br /> <br /> Right, the level of darkness depends on where in the Union the PCs are placed. At it's best it is similar to the Men in Black movies. As a general things, it falls somewhere between the movies 1984 and Brazil. At the lower end it is all too similar to the film, The Grey Zone. It starts for the PCs well meaning, but everything gradually and steadily becomes worse and they become ever more compromised. <br /> <br /> I also think the leadership of the Union is fatally compromised by the Nephandi. By way of comparison, someone who has fatal cancer is not composed mostly of cancer cells - the cancer has just destroyed enough of vital systems to kill the person. Likewise, the Union is not composed of mostly Nephadi, but there are enough of them and they are in the right position to doom the Union.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T10:32:11-08:00","id":1467173,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm not terribly fond of the Nephandic infiltration narrative, as it can be seen as absolving the Union of its own failures: \u201cwe're not to blame; it's the Fallen who took over Control who have made such a mess of things.\u201d (though to be fair, the Nephandi wouldn't be able to do half the damage that they do if their victims weren't so corruptible.)<br /> <br /> I <i>am</i>, however, fond of the idea that the Technocracy has a problem with Denial, brought on by their reliance on Conditioning. This can range from the Rose-colored Mirrorshades that <b>Guide to the Technocracy</b> mentioned to the occasional cases of \u201cmagic isn't real!\u201d \u2014 with the latter occasionally going into full-blown Negation Men territory. And all too many of the Technocrats who <i>aren't</i> in Denial don't see a problem with this \u2014 at least, not one severe enough to do anything about. Heck, there are Technocrats who know about the Negation Men in their ranks and view them as a sort of <i>asset</i>, a weapon that can be used against the Superstitionists. <br /> <br /> <i>That's</i> not so much a matter of the Technocracy being \u201cdark\u201d (as in, corrupt) as it is about them being\u2026 not entirely in their right minds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-08-2021, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T11:04:53-08:00","id":1467184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1466786#post1466786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to Malcolm Sheppard (MRev), the celestial chorus never was the driving force between Christianity or Islam. It was always a heresy. Likewise, according to Malcolm, with every Tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's basically my take on them as well, but it makes them a very odd fit. It both limits their historical role in the game and changes the philosophical differences they had with the other pre-Traditions. <br /> <br /> When I think of the idea of the Traditions I expect that one of them should be some kind of ecumenical alliance. That's missing, though, and instead there's an ancient gnostic/theosophical/monist conspiracy. I like the ancient gnostic/theosophical/monist conspiracy, but at best it should be there in addition to the eccumenical alliance. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1467014#post1467014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think the leadership of the Union is fatally compromised by the Nephandi. By way of comparison, someone who has fatal cancer is not composed mostly of cancer cells - the cancer has just destroyed enough of vital systems to kill the person. Likewise, the Union is not composed of mostly Nephadi, but there are enough of them and they are in the right position to doom the Union.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Nephandi has one of the best PR teams around. If something goes foul, they will claim credit for it. Whether they are actually responsible for it or not is another matter.<br /> That being said, I find it very important that the Technocracy be monstrous in their own right. The Nephandi can be making them worse, or pushing them to be more brazen, or in some way exacerbating the situation, but the problems have to be there from the start.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T12:43:07-08:00","id":1467191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you?p=1467184#post1467184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Nephandi can be making them worse, or pushing them to be more brazen, or in some way exacerbating the situation, but the problems have to be there from the start.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is my view of both groups, the Union and the Nephandi. The Nephandi enable horror and exacerbate problems and pain, and they do not have to create either. And the Union is rooted many problems and evil, such as genocide and totalitarian methods. The Nephandi just put some work into making certain the Union never does better.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}